### B.13 §3.5 Badge — stroke rev path

The current "uniformly borderless across every tone" rule (§3.5 audit table) arrived via two dropped revs:

1. **Rev A — `border/subtle` (150) across all tones** (May 2026 audit). Rationale was "fix the only fill-tinted contained surface without a definition stroke." The rev made Badge M visually indistinguishable from Button XS soft at the height-collision case (both 24-tall, both with 1px stroke, both with tonal soft fill) — Badge-vs-Button differentiation collapsed.
2. **Rev B — neutral keeps stroke, tonal goes borderless**. Solved the Badge-vs-Button collision geometrically (tonal Badge now had zero stroke vs Button's 1px stroke) but read as inconsistent across the Badge family — neutral Badge had a visible edge while tonal Badge didn't, making tonal Badges feel less defined than their neutral sibling.
3. **Current — uniform borderless across all tones**. Prioritizes Badge-family consistency and accepts that neutral reads softer-edged than tonal. Industry alignment: shadcn `secondary` Badge / Atlassian default Lozenge / Vercel neutral Tag all ship neutral-borderless for the same reason — the family identity matters more than the individual edge-crispness of the quietest variant.

