### §B.44 Field/Fieldset text elements — strip the 2px H drift from labels, captions, and legends (May 20, 2026)

#### The symptom

A `Form` variant dialog showed the inner `Label` text visibly 2px farther inset than the `Title` and `Description` above it, despite the user expectation that they all share an x-baseline since they're all text rows inside the same dialog padding.

User observation: "why does the text here not align, despite having the same 2px padding applied to both? it looks like the label text is more inset."

#### Root cause — the same double-counting pattern §B.41 fixed, just one layer deeper

`.ds-field__label` carries its own `padding: 0 var(--space-3xs, 2px)` declaration. When the label sits inside a Dialog body, the H paddings stack:

| Element | Layer 1 | Layer 2 | Layer 3 | Total H inset from outer dialog edge |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Dialog title | `--dlg-px` (12) on `.ds-dialog` | `--dlg-text-px` (2) on `.ds-dialog__header-text` | title itself (0) | **14px** ✓ |
| Dialog description | `--dlg-px` (12) | `--dlg-text-px` (2) on `__header-text` | description itself (0) | **14px** ✓ |
| Field label inside body | `--dlg-px` (12) | `--dlg-text-px` (2) on `.ds-dialog__body` | **`.ds-field__label` padding (2)** | **16px** ✗ — 2px off |

§B.41 fixed the wrapper-and-direct-child case (dialog title + header wrapper both adding 2px). This case is the same pattern, one nesting level deeper: the dialog body's 2px wrapper combines with the field label's 2px to produce 4px instead of 2px.

#### Why the 2px H on field text was drift in the first place

§6.1.4 says the H direction has NO leading delta — the 2px H pattern only makes sense for V leading absorption, not H. The 2px H padding on `.ds-field__label` is just drift. It also misaligns the label in the **standalone** case (field outside any dialog/card):

- Label cap-top sits at 2px H from the field's left edge
- Input border sits at 0px H from the field's left edge
- Label is therefore 2px inset from the input's border — which contradicts the industry convention (Apple HIG / Material 3 / shadcn / Atlassian / Primer all align label flush with input border)

Removing the 2px H fixes both contexts:
- Standalone: label sits flush with input border ✓ industry-aligned
- In dialog: label sits at 14px H from outer (same as title and description) ✓ baseline-aligned

#### The fix

Removed `padding: 0 var(--space-3xs, 2px)` from four field/fieldset text elements in `index.html`:

| Element | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| `.ds-field__label` | `... padding: 0 var(--space-3xs,2px)` | (no padding declared) |
| `.ds-field__caption` | `... padding: 0 var(--space-3xs,2px)` | (no padding declared) |
| `.ds-fieldset__legend` | `... padding: 0 var(--space-3xs,2px)` | (no padding declared) |
| `.ds-fieldset__caption` | `... padding: 0 var(--space-3xs,2px)` | (no padding declared) |
| `.ds-fieldset__validation` | `... padding: 0 var(--space-3xs,2px)` | (no padding declared) |

Each text element now sits flush with its parent's content-area edge. When the parent is a standalone `.ds-field`, that's the input's outer border. When the parent is `.ds-dialog__body` (which carries its own 2px H wrapper padding), the text sits at 14px H — same baseline as title and description.

#### Cross-component audit

Re-ran a grep for `padding:0 var(--space-3xs` across `index.html` to identify any remaining text-inside-wrapper drift:

- `.ds-dialog__title`, `.ds-dialog__description` — fixed in §B.41
- `.ds-card__title`, `.ds-card__description` — fixed in §B.41
- `.ds-field__label`, `.ds-field__caption`, `.ds-fieldset__legend`, `.ds-fieldset__caption`, `.ds-fieldset__validation` — fixed in §B.44 (this section)

Other matches (Button, Badge, Nav, Breadcrumb, Segmented Control, Date Picker, Checkbox/Radio/Switch rows, Select, Menu, Tabs, Chip) are single-layer applications — the 2px H sits on the leaf text element and is not nested inside another wrapper that also adds H padding. Those remain as the canonical "text element sits 2px inside its own backplate" pattern. No further fixes needed in this pass.

#### Comprehensive thoroughness audit (May 20, 2026, follow-up)

After the field/fieldset fix, the user requested an explicit thoroughness pass: "make sure this is not happening anywhere else, where there are multiple layers of 2px padding being applied. be thorough."

The audit identified every CSS rule containing `padding: ... var(--space-3xs` in `index.html` (28 total) and mapped each to its parent context to classify it as either **WRAPPER** (a flex/grid container holding text or wrappable children) or **LEAF** (the terminal text node or icon SVG host):

**All seven WRAPPER candidates verified after the fix:**

| Wrapper | H padding | Child elements | Stacking risk? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.ds-dialog__header-text` | 2px | `__title`, `__description` (both 0 padding after §B.41) | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-dialog__body` | 2px (`--dlg-text-px`) | `<p>`, `<h*>`, `.ds-field`, `.ds-fieldset` (field elements now 0 padding) | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-card__header-text` | 2px | `__title`, `__description` (both 0 padding after §B.41) | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-card__body` | 2px | Any content; field elements now 0 padding | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-toast__body` | 2px (`--tst-body-px`) | `__title`, `__description` (both 0 padding by design) | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-banner__body` | 4px (`--bn-body-px`) | `__title`, `__description` (both 0 padding by design) | ✓ clean |
| `.ds-tooltip__text` | 4px (`--tt-body-px`) | None — leaf text node | ✓ clean (no children) |

**All 21 LEAF candidates verified single-layer (no stacking risk):**

Button (`__label`), Badge (`__label`), Nav (`__label`), Bottom Nav (`__label`), Breadcrumb (`__label`), Segmented Control (`__label`), Date Picker (`__title` — month/year header), Drop Zone (`__title`, `__hint`), Drop Zone File (`__icon` — SVG host, 2px all sides), Checkbox/Radio/Switch row (`__label`, `__description`), Radio Card (`__label`, `__description`), Select (`__value`, `__placeholder`), Select Panel (`__text`), Select Panel & Menu (`__group-label` — uses `calc(item-px + 2)` to align with item content, single layer), Menu (`__label`), Tabs (`__label`), Chip (`__label`).

Every leaf sits directly inside its parent backplate's H padding (typically `--{comp}-px` at 6/8/12/16). The 2px H on the leaf is the canonical "text element sits 2px inside its own backplate" pattern, intentional, single-layer, no stacking.

**Special cases reviewed:**
- `.ds-fieldset__required { margin-left: 2px }` — 2px LEFT margin on the asterisk glyph inside a legend; sits beside legend text, not nested under it. No stacking.
- `.ds-fieldset__items { gap: var(--space-3xs, 2px) }` — `gap`, not padding. No stacking.
- `.ds-toast__body { gap: var(--space-3xs, 2px) }`, `.ds-banner__body { gap: var(--space-3xs, 2px) }`, `.ds-card__header-text { gap: 0 }`, `.ds-radio-card__text { gap: var(--space-3xs, 2px) }` — `gap` values on flex columns separating title from description; not padding, no stacking.
- `.ds-tooltip { gap: calc(var(--space-s, 8px) - var(--tt-body-px)) }` — clever subtraction to keep visible inter-child gap at 8px when both children have 4px own-padding. Intentional offset; not a stacking issue.

**Conclusion**: the only "multiple 2px layers" pattern in the system was the dialog/card title-description-fieldlabel chain documented in §B.41 + §B.44. After this fix, every wrapper carries the 2px on behalf of its text children; every text leaf either sits inside such a wrapper (with its own padding zeroed) OR sits directly inside a backplate that uses a non-2px padding (in which case its 2px is single-layer and intentional). The system is clean.

#### Lesson — the drift pattern is "two consecutive layers both add 2px H"

§B.41 framed this as a Dialog/Card-specific bug. §B.44 shows it's a system-level pattern: any text element with `padding: 0 var(--space-3xs)` that's then placed inside a wrapper that ALSO has `padding: 0 var(--space-3xs)` will be 2px off. The rule going forward:

- Wrapper containers (`.ds-dialog__body`, `.ds-dialog__header-text`, `.ds-card__header`, etc.) own the 2px H wrapper inset on behalf of their text content.
- Leaf text elements (`__title`, `__description`, `__label`, `__caption`, `__legend`) do NOT carry their own H padding when they're typically used inside such wrappers.
- Standalone text components (Button labels, Badge text, Nav item labels) that sit directly inside the component's main backplate keep their own H padding because there's no double-wrapper to combine with.

