## Part C — Cross-system audit snapshots used to derive current rules

### C.1 Bottom Nav single-size industry audit (May 2026)

| System | Component | Container height | Sizes shipped |
|---|---|---|---|
| Apple HIG | Tab Bar (iOS) | 49pt (fixed) | One |
| Apple HIG | Tab Bar (iOS 18 floating) | ~50pt pill | One |
| Material 3 | Navigation Bar | 80dp | One (NavigationRail is a *separate component* for tablet) |
| Notion (mobile) | (custom) | ~60pt | One |
| X / Twitter (mobile) | (custom) | ~50pt | One |
| Primer (GitHub) | — | — | Doesn't ship one |
| shadcn | — | — | Doesn't ship one |

Industry consensus is **unequivocally one size**. A "dense" or "comfortable" bottom nav doesn't make sense for the role — there's no use case for shrinking the primary navigation in a mobile app. Multiple sizes invite consumers to pick the wrong tier and accidentally produce a harder-to-tap bar.

### C.2 Tabs vs Segmented Control — hover-indicator audit

| System | Tabs hover treatment | Segmented Control hover treatment |
|---|---|---|
| shadcn | Backplate bg fill | Pill fill |
| Atlassian | Backplate bg fill | Pill fill |
| Linear | Underbar shape (gray) | Pill fill |
| Vercel Geist | Underbar shape (gray) | Pill fill |
| Stripe | Underbar shape (gray) | Pill fill |
| Apple HIG (older) | Underbar shape (gray) | Pill fill |
| Material 3 | Underbar (both states) | Pill fill |
| Primer | Underbar (both states) | Pill fill |

Industry is split for Tabs hover (backplate vs underbar) but unanimous for Segmented Control (pill). Our system sits with the underbar-hover camp because it produces a cleaner three-way differentiation across our horizontal-trigger families (Segmented Control / Tabs / Button) with no cross-component grammar reread.

### C.3 Pagination active-style audit

| System | Active treatment | Inactive treatment | Prev/Next |
|---|---|---|---|
| shadcn Pagination | `outline` button (outlined, with stronger border) | `ghost` button | Icon + text label by default |
| GitHub Primer Pagination | `default` (neutral filled) | Bare link | Icon-only |
| Vercel Geist Pagination | Filled black (`solid-neutral`) | Bare text | Icon-only chevrons |
| Atlassian Pagination | Filled brand (`solid-brand`) | Bare text | Icon-only |
| Material 3 Pagination | Filled brand-tonal surface | Text button | Icon-only |
| Linear | Filled neutral with brand text | Ghost | Icon-only |
| Tailwind UI Pagination | Saturated `solid-brand` | Bare text | Icon-only chevrons |
| **Ours (default preset)** | **`soft-brand` chip with `--btn-br` overridden to `selection/border` (blue/300)** | **`outline-neutral` with `--btn-br` overridden to `border/subtle` (neutral/150)** | **Icon-only `outline-neutral` matching rest stroke override** |
| **Ours (filled preset)** | `solid-brand` (saturated brand-500 fill + white text + standard luminous-edge rim) | `soft-neutral` (`neutral/50` fill + `neutral/100` hairline + neutral text) | Icon-only `soft-neutral` |

The default preset doesn't fit cleanly in the industry table because no major system pairs an outlined-rest with an outlined-active distinguished only by stroke color. shadcn `Pagination`'s "active = `outline` variant + ghost inactive" is the closest analog (both use the outline shape language) but shadcn keeps rest as ghost; we promote rest to outline so the row carries strokes everywhere. The filled preset lands squarely in the Tailwind UI / Atlassian saturated-brand lane.
